ist\n\\item\n  \\textbf{Document (MongoDB)}: Storing JSON-like data for flexible\n  schemas.\\\\\n\\item\n  \\textbf{Columnar (Cassandra)}: High write-throughput for time-series\n  data.\\\\\n\\item\n  \\textbf{Graph (Neo4j)}: Managing complex relationships in social\n  networks.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\n\\textbf{Q22:} What is the primary advantage of \\textbf{in-memory\ndatabases}?\\\\\n\\emph{Answer:} In-memory databases store data in RAM, enabling faster\naccess and processing compared to disk-based systems.\n\n\\textbf{Q23:} How does a \\textbf{time series database} differ from a\ntraditional relational database?\\\\\n\\emph{Answer:} Time series databases are optimized for storing and\nquerying time-stamped data, while relational databases focus on\nstructured, transactional data.\n\n\\textbf{Q24:} What is the main benefit of using \\textbf{DBaaS} (Database\nas a Service)?\\\\\n\\emph{Answer:} DBaaS reduces infrastructure management, offers\npay-as-you-go pricing, and provides scalability and global availability.\n\n\\textbf{Q25:} Explain why \\textbf{NoSQL databases} are often preferred\nfor big data applications.\\\\\n\\emph{Answer:} NoSQL databases offer flexible schemas, horizontal\nscalability, and high availability, making them ideal for handling\nunstructured or semi-structured big data.\n\n\\begin{center}\\rule{0.5\\linewidth}{0.5pt}\\end{center}\n\nLet me know if you need further clarification! 😊\n\n\\end{document}\n"
